   304→          <h2>About the 2D Graphics Engine</h2>
   305→
   306→          <h3>What is this?</h3>
   307→          <p>
   308→            This is a <strong>2D graphics API</strong> similar to OpenGL, but focused on 2D rendering instead of 3D. Just like OpenGL provides functions for drawing triangles and applying textures in 3D space, this engine provides a complete API for 2D drawing operations.
   309→          </p>
   310→          <p>
   311→            It's a software renderer built from scratch in C++, implementing functionality found in production libraries like <strong>Skia</strong> (used by Chrome and Android), <strong>Cairo</strong> (used by GTK and Firefox), and the <strong>HTML5 Canvas API</strong>. You give it high-level drawing commands—"draw a rectangle," "fill a path with a gradient," "apply a matrix transformation"—and it produces the actual pixel colors on screen.
   312→          </p>
   313→          <p>
   314→            <strong>Key Features:</strong>
   315→          </p>
   316→          <ul style={{ lineHeight: 1.8, color: '#555' }}>
